Among these, *serum B12 and TSH* are universally available, inexpensive, and frequently abnormal in mimics of primary psychosis. B12 deficiency can present insidiously with psychiatric symptoms before anemia or neuropathy appears. TSH is equally critical — both are part of standard medical workup for new-onset psychosis.

I’ll request B12 first — it’s more likely than thyroid disease to present with isolated psychiatric features early on.

